            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Kneedler, section\u202f1101(a)(43)(B) of the Immigration and Nationality Act incorporates that definition, so a conviction that meets the federal drug\u2011trafficking definition can trigger immigration consequences."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e3765dd5a716713bc161ee2666a85786ef7809d8ce4dbc68a524e2779d3fd43c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e3765dd5a716-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 60,
              "start": 60
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "An aggravated\u2011felony conviction can bar a non\u2011citizen from becoming a U.S. citizen because it forecloses the ability to establish good moral character."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
